=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — periodic network "freezes" affecting the entire campus — was investigated across all four diagnostic phases with no confirming evidence found.

Phase 1 reachability showed 0% packet loss across all 28 tested src→dst pairs. Phase A infrastructure sweep flagged no ACL rules, no addressing anomalies, no ARP conflicts, and no resolver divergence across all 15 hosts. The l2_snapshot duplicate-MAC hits (0.0.0.0 and ::) are a known false positive from Linux kernel tunnel interfaces (tunl0, sit0, gre0) present on every host by design.

Phase B found OSPF fully converged across all 9 routers: 9/9 vtysh healthy, all neighbors in Full/DR or Full/Backup state, 17 OSPF routes consistent everywhere. The tc_snapshot found only default pfifo_fast qdiscs on all reachable interfaces — no shaping, no netem, no tbf.

Phase D pressure sweep returned no suspect devices; no stress tool, CPU spike, or socket exhaustion was present on any device.

To rule out the intermittent mechanism specifically: no flap script or periodic process was found on any core device (router7, router16, router17, mswitch0). All active OSPF-facing interfaces showed carrier_changes = 2, which is the startup-only baseline in Kathara (one down→up transition at container launch). No syslog entries recording OSPF reconvergence, adjacency drops, or link state changes were present.

Root cause: no fault is present. The reported freezing symptom has no mechanism, no carrier history, and no syslog trace — it is unconfirmed by any observable evidence in the current live topology.

Fix: no corrective action required. If the symptom recurs, capture syslog (`journalctl -k` or `/var/log/syslog`) and carrier_changes counters on the core routers immediately after an episode.
=== END ===